{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>The widget's own third parties, and how to actually verify the fix</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      Don't stop at the vendor you chose, some widgets pull in their own analytics or error-tracking scripts, which are additional third parties your CSP also has to account for. If your <code>connect-src</code> only allowlists the main widget domain, a second script it loads can still get blocked (good) or, if you widen the policy carelessly to make it stop erroring, silently allowed (bad). Check the widget vendor's docs for a list of every domain their script talks to, not just their main one.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Verify the fix by actually opening DevTools → Network while the widget loads, filter by the widget's domain, and read the request payloads, don't assume the sandbox worked because there were no console errors. A sandboxed iframe with <code>allow-scripts</code> but no <code>allow-same-origin</code> will throw if the widget's own code tries something that needs same-origin access, which is useful signal: if you see no errors and no unexpected payload contents, that's your actual verification, not the absence of a red console line.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Two things worth pinning down beyond the initial setup: Subresource Integrity (<code>integrity="sha384-…"</code> on the script tag) so a compromised or silently-updated vendor script can't change behavior under you without the browser refusing to execute it, though most AI widget vendors ship frequently-changing bundles that make a hash-pinned SRI value impractical to maintain, in which case pinning to a versioned URL rather than a "latest" alias is the realistic middle ground. And check the vendor's data-use terms specifically for whether page content sent as "context" is used for model training by default, that's a separate question from where the data is stored, and it's the one most likely to matter for a compliance review.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

