{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A third-party widget script tag runs with the same DOM and cookie access as your own code — it can read whatever's visible on the page and send it to its own backend, with nothing in the browser stopping it by default.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">CSP's connect-src limits where any script can send data, a sandboxed iframe (allow-scripts, no allow-same-origin) stops the widget reading your page's DOM and cookies at all, and an explicit field allowlist stops your own integration code from handing it more than it needs.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Check what other domains the widget's own script calls, verify the fix by reading actual network payloads in DevTools rather than trusting the absence of console errors, and confirm whether the vendor uses page content sent as "context" for model training by default.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
